1358
01:14:44,105 --> 01:14:46,148
People forget we're live.
You like the window,
don't you?

1359
01:14:46,232 --> 01:14:47,315
Yeah!

1360
01:14:47,400 --> 01:14:49,651
Joe, before we wrap this up,
is there anything else
you wanna say?

1361
01:14:49,777 --> 01:14:51,236
I just wanna say thanks
to all the people that

1362
01:14:51,320 --> 01:14:54,447
stop me in the street
and tell me my story
helped them somehow.

1363
01:14:54,615 --> 01:14:58,243
And your story is really cool.
It's like a Behind the Music
without the music.

1364
01:14:58,327 --> 01:15:01,413
But are you depressed
I mean, your parents,
who you were looking for,

1365
01:15:02,081 --> 01:15:06,501
all along, were dead.
Was the last decade
a complete waste?

1366
01:15:06,586 --> 01:15:09,671
Well, uh, no one's
really put it like that,
but I don't think so.

1367
01:15:09,755 --> 01:15:13,967
I've had some good times,
met some cool people, cruised
around, cranked some tunes.

1368
01:15:14,177 --> 01:15:16,636
What about Brandy
Is there any chance you guys
are gonna hook back up?

1369
01:15:16,721 --> 01:15:20,849
Um, well, you know,
she's a good friend of mine,
and she's off doin'

1370
01:15:21,267 --> 01:15:24,186
her own thing right now,
but I've always said
she's a little too hot

1371
01:15:24,270 --> 01:15:27,230
for old Joe Dirt.
I agree.
So does America.

1372
01:15:27,315 --> 01:15:30,358
In fact, in our latest
"Is Brandy too hot
for Joe Dirt?" poll,

1373
01:15:30,443 --> 01:15:35,405
61 % of you agreed.
Even worse, 4% said the dog
was too hot for you.

1374
01:15:35,948 --> 01:15:38,617
Dang.
I'm just kidding.
You're on TRL, California.

1375
01:15:38,743 --> 01:15:39,993
Hello, California.

1376
01:15:40,286 --> 01:15:43,413
WOMAN: Hey, wait... Am I ...
Am I on? I'm on?

1377
01:15:43,748 --> 01:15:48,793
Hey, baby, I'm on!
Yeah. Hey, Carson,
how big's your Johnny?

1378
01:15:48,878 --> 01:15:52,339
Joe, I think happy hour
started a little early
in California.

1379
01:15:52,465 --> 01:15:56,426
A little drinky-drinky.
The reason I'm really callin'
is Joe Dirt's parents

1380
01:15:56,510 --> 01:16:01,556
ain't dead.
I'm lookin' at his father
right now, and I'm his mama.

1381
01:16:01,682 --> 01:16:05,477
Ma'am, you should never
drink the bong water.
Yeah, listen to him.

1382
01:16:05,978 --> 01:16:09,147
Carson, just where you
wanna be when Jesus
comes back?

1383
01:16:09,232 --> 01:16:10,649
Makin' fun...
Sorry, Joe.

1384
01:16:10,775 --> 01:16:14,152
Wait, wait. Where's that
call comin' from?
California.

1385
01:16:14,487 --> 01:16:15,862
Listen, I gotta go.

1386
01:16:15,988 --> 01:16:17,364
Oh, no, Joe!

1387
01:16:17,782 --> 01:16:19,449
So, Carson helped me
trace the call,

1388
01:16:19,533 --> 01:16:22,827
and it led me
to this old trailer park
in Simi Valley, California.

1389
01:16:25,665 --> 01:16:28,750
Wow. Wow.

1390
01:16:33,172 --> 01:16:34,881
That's our old car!

1391
01:16:36,342 --> 01:16:38,551
Right here, guys.
There he is.

1392
01:16:39,345 --> 01:16:43,098
WOMAN : Joe, can I have
an exclusive?

1393
01:16:43,557 --> 01:16:45,684
Your parents
are alive after all?

1394
01:16:46,686 --> 01:16:48,853
Joe! Joe!
How are you feeling?

1395
01:16:50,022 --> 01:16:51,815
DIRT: Mom, Dad, is that you?

1396
01:16:53,609 --> 01:16:55,568
Our baby's home.

1397
01:16:56,612 --> 01:16:59,614
Damn. We tried
so hard to find him.
We looked high and low.

1398
01:16:59,699 --> 01:17:02,867
I got some pictures here.
Look at this.
Here's a picture of Joe

1399
01:17:03,035 --> 01:17:05,954
when he was a baby.
Did you get it?
Yeah. Aw, baby.

1400
01:17:06,414 --> 01:17:09,207
You were a cute baby,
Joe Dirt.
That's why we were so crazy

1401
01:17:09,292 --> 01:17:12,419
when we lost him.
I mean, he's here
and now he's gone.

1402
01:17:12,545 --> 01:17:15,922
Oh, mama,
it's all right.
Where'd he go? Aw.

1403
01:17:16,674 --> 01:17:18,383
Did they get it?
Oh, where'd he go?

1404
01:17:18,676 --> 01:17:20,927
I was at the canyon, yeah.
You know what?

1405
01:17:21,053 --> 01:17:24,389
It was right by
the garbage can
where you left me.

1406
01:17:25,391 --> 01:17:28,393
Wha...? Is that
where you were?
Well, I'll be dipped.

1407
01:17:28,894 --> 01:17:31,396
The one place
we didn't look.
I knew you looked for me.

1408
01:17:31,480 --> 01:17:34,691
I told everybody you would.
And was there ever a time

1409
01:17:34,775 --> 01:17:37,527
when you would look
at the moon,
and was hopin' maybe

1410
01:17:37,611 --> 01:17:38,695
I was lookin' at it too?

1411
01:17:38,821 --> 01:17:39,904
Wouldn't you know

1412
01:17:40,031 --> 01:17:42,991
that I've been doin'
this clown sort of thing?
Can everybody get a shot

1413
01:17:43,075 --> 01:17:46,036
of these? Do you see
these clown figurines?
Whenever I used to get sad,

1414
01:17:46,120 --> 01:17:51,291
I'd just look at a clown,
and then I just can't help it.
I just can't stop grinnin'.

1415
01:17:51,375 --> 01:17:52,625
They're available
for purchase.

1416
01:17:52,752 --> 01:17:54,836
We're startin' this
Clown.com kind of a thing.

1417
01:17:54,920 --> 01:17:55,920
Yeah.

1418
01:17:56,047 --> 01:17:58,882
I don't mean to interrupt
your clown pitch there,

1419
01:17:59,091 --> 01:18:04,679
but how exactly do you not
go right back to the place
where you saw me?

1420
01:18:05,348 --> 01:18:07,932
(NEWS CREW MUTTERING)

1421
01:18:08,225 --> 01:18:11,519
Hey, how exactly
is a rainbow made?

1422
01:18:11,604 --> 01:18:13,438
How exactly
does the sun set?

1423
01:18:13,564 --> 01:18:16,274
How exactly does
the Posi-Trac rear end
on a Plymouth work?

1424
01:18:17,568 --> 01:18:18,610
It just does.

1425
01:18:18,778 --> 01:18:19,819
It just does.

1426
01:18:19,904 --> 01:18:21,529
I'm not talkin'
about Posi-Trac.

1427
01:18:21,614 --> 01:18:26,534
I'm talkin' about me.
How long did you look for me
before you gave up?

1428
01:18:26,619 --> 01:18:29,287
How long were you
ridin' in that car before
you realized I wasn't in it?

1429
01:18:29,372 --> 01:18:31,331
Exactly how long?

1430
01:18:38,297 --> 01:18:40,840
All right!
We didn't lose him.

1431
01:18:40,925 --> 01:18:44,344
We just left him.
So what?
The dude's doin' fine!

1432
01:18:44,470 --> 01:18:45,637
Look at him!

1433
01:18:45,721 --> 01:18:47,889
How could you do that to me?
I was only eight years old.

1434
01:18:47,973 --> 01:18:51,935
I was just a little kid.
Do you have any idea
what it's like to be a kid and

1435
01:18:52,019 --> 01:18:56,856
have nobody around to talk to?
No one that cares
if you're alive or dead?

1436
01:18:57,817 --> 01:19:01,403
Every day you just think
you're worthless, and there's
a void in your life.

1437
01:19:01,529 --> 01:19:04,489
Oh, come on, honey.
Lose that frown!
Lighten up, buddy.

1438
01:19:05,241 --> 01:19:07,700
When you're down,
stare at a clown.

1439
01:19:07,785 --> 01:19:10,620
Hey, sit down! You're
blockin' the cameras!
Move over.

1440
01:19:10,704 --> 01:19:14,791
I don't care about that!
And I don't care
about you!

1441
01:19:16,669 --> 01:19:20,213
And I don't wanna see you
for another 25 years!
Joe, wait!

1442
01:19:20,297 --> 01:19:23,591
I wish he'd never found us!
Look what he did
to my children!

1443
01:19:23,676 --> 01:19:24,884
Hey, TV people!

1444
01:19:24,969 --> 01:19:29,097
Hey, you're grounded!
Hey, TV people!
Why are y'all goin' away?

1445
01:19:29,181 --> 01:19:32,016
Come over here!
You don't have to follow him!

1446
01:19:32,101 --> 01:19:34,394
(REPORTERS SHOUTING QUESTIONS)

1447
01:19:38,357 --> 01:19:39,774
MAN : What are you gonna
do now, Joe?

1448
01:19:51,412 --> 01:19:54,914
MAN : Somebody do something.

1449
01:19:56,167 --> 01:20:01,671
WOMAN :
Joe, just turn around now.
It's not worth it, Joe.

1450
01:20:02,381 --> 01:20:06,134
(HELICOPTER WHIRRING)
REPORTER: We are here at
Wallace Bridge,

1451
01:20:06,218 --> 01:20:09,762
where local celebrity Joe Dirt
is threatening
to kill himself.

1452
01:20:10,222 --> 01:20:13,349
Come on, Joe.
Remember what you said
on the show,

1453
01:20:13,434 --> 01:20:15,727
"Life's a garden.
Dig it?"

1454
01:20:16,395 --> 01:20:19,731
You gotta get down from there,
brother. You don't wanna
do this.

1455
01:20:21,108 --> 01:20:23,985
Why not, man,
I got nothin'.
I've been lookin' forever

1456
01:20:24,069 --> 01:20:27,363
for those people, and everyone
lies to me, man.

1457
01:20:28,532 --> 01:20:30,158
I'm worthless.

1458
01:20:31,952 --> 01:20:32,952
Joe!

1459
01:20:34,330 --> 01:20:35,330
Joe!

1460
01:20:36,290 --> 01:20:40,502
Hey, sorry, lady. You can't
cut through here.
Joe, it's me, Brandy!

1461
01:20:40,586 --> 01:20:42,837
Oh, it's Brandy?
Like, the Brandy?
Yes!

1462
01:20:43,214 --> 01:20:45,423
Why didn't you say so.
Come on!

1463
01:20:45,508 --> 01:20:47,842
Hey, everybody, Brandy's here!
Hey, it's Brandy!

1464
01:20:49,595 --> 01:20:50,595
Come on, come on.

1465
01:20:51,013 --> 01:20:52,013
That's her!

1466
01:20:52,848 --> 01:20:54,015
Joe!

1467
01:20:54,308 --> 01:20:55,433
Brandy?

1468
01:20:56,018 --> 01:20:56,976
I'm here, Joe.

1469
01:20:57,436 --> 01:21:00,188
You told me my parents
were dead, and I saw 'em.

1470
01:21:00,314 --> 01:21:02,815
They're horrible.
Why did you lie to me?

1471
01:21:03,108 --> 01:21:07,028
They saw you on the news
when you saved those kids.
They thought you got a reward.

1472
01:21:07,488 --> 01:21:10,532
So you did see 'em first.
So it's just like
Robby said.

1473
01:21:10,616 --> 01:21:14,536
Yes, but once I met them,
I knew I had to
protect you from them.

1474
01:21:14,954 --> 01:21:18,498
They're bad people.
You're not
like them, Joe.

1475
01:21:19,542 --> 01:21:23,503
They didn't leave you.
You left them.
You've gotta see that.

1476
01:21:24,588 --> 01:21:27,423
And, Joe, if you had
stayed with them,
you wouldn't have turned out

1477
01:21:27,508 --> 01:21:28,716
as wonderful as you are.

1478
01:21:28,968 --> 01:21:31,511
Robby said
you didn't want me around,

1479
01:21:31,595 --> 01:21:34,430
and he said that you was
always laughin' at me
behind my back.

1480
01:21:34,640 --> 01:21:38,309
Why would Robby say
such a thing?
Of course that's not true.

1481
01:21:38,644 --> 01:21:42,730
I love you, Joe,
with all my heart.

1482
01:21:43,983 --> 01:21:48,570
I wanna get married, Joe,
and have little Joe Dirts.
Come home, Joe.

1483
01:21:49,363 --> 01:21:52,824
You had a home all along.
You just couldn't see it.

1484
01:21:52,992 --> 01:21:54,158
(NEIGHING)

1485
01:21:54,410 --> 01:21:55,994
You really love me?

1486
01:21:56,161 --> 01:21:59,289
(CROWD CHEERING)

1487
01:22:02,793 --> 01:22:05,169
I did it! I did it!
I roped him
with a bungee cord.

1488
01:22:10,301 --> 01:22:11,217
No!

1489
01:22:11,885 --> 01:22:13,595
Dang!

1490
01:22:13,887 --> 01:22:15,888
Joe! Joe!

1491
01:22:17,474 --> 01:22:18,516
Ooh!

1492
01:22:18,642 --> 01:22:20,101
(ALL GROAN)

1493
01:22:35,159 --> 01:22:37,619
Oh, man. I just had
the weirdest dream.

1494
01:22:38,120 --> 01:22:39,537
You were in it.

1495
01:22:40,039 --> 01:22:41,456
So were you.

1496
01:22:44,376 --> 01:22:47,086
Oh, my God.
Brandy, I'm home?

1497
01:22:48,505 --> 01:22:50,882
Clem, Charlene,
Kickin' Wing.

1498
01:22:51,216 --> 01:22:52,550
It's not Clem anymore.

1499
01:22:53,135 --> 01:22:54,427
It's Gert B. Frobe.

1500
01:22:54,553 --> 01:22:55,762
Wha?

1501
01:22:55,888 --> 01:22:57,930
Witness Protection relocated
me. I asked for Silvertown,

1502
01:22:58,057 --> 01:23:01,100
on account of how you
talked about it.
It's wonderful here.

1503
01:23:01,352 --> 01:23:03,144
Hello, Joe Dirt.

1504
01:23:03,228 --> 01:23:06,606
You taught me
to sell the good stuff.
Now I have

1505
01:23:06,690 --> 01:23:11,402
30 fireworks stands,
which completely fund
my animal shelters.

1506
01:23:11,779 --> 01:23:13,112
It's all because of you, Joe.

1507
01:23:13,530 --> 01:23:14,864
Good job, brother.

1508
01:23:14,990 --> 01:23:18,910
I sold the gator farm, after
one of those bastards snapped
off my thumb

1509
01:23:18,994 --> 01:23:22,413
and middle finger. I came up
here to check up on you,
and, well,

1510
01:23:22,539 --> 01:23:24,832
I met Gert B. Frobe.

1511
01:23:26,418 --> 01:23:28,252
And it's a good thing
that gator didn't get
my ring finger,

1512
01:23:28,337 --> 01:23:30,129
because Gert's asked me
to marry him.

1513
01:23:30,214 --> 01:23:31,214
Yeah.

1514
01:23:32,007 --> 01:23:33,883
Right on.
Joe.

1515
01:23:34,301 --> 01:23:37,595
When you were in the hospital
for your head injury,
I had the doctor

1516
01:23:37,680 --> 01:23:41,224
